The test method rebuilds the `Dropout` layer each run with the same arguments: `rate=0.35`, `noise_shape=(1, 6)`, and `seed=2718`, then makes exactly one training-time forward call. In `Dropout`, that fixed integer seed is wrapped in a new `SeedGenerator`, and `call()` passes it to `backend.random.dropout`. `SeedGenerator` starts from the same initial state for the same seed and returns that initial seed value on its first use, so the first dropout mask generated by the backend is the same every time a fresh layer is created. Because the inputs and configuration are unchanged, the resulting `output_tensor` is identical across repeated executions of this test.

